NAME
       initctl, systemctl - control the init service manager

SYNOPSIS
       **initctl** __command__ [__unit__...]

DESCRIPTION
       A unit name without a suffix means NAME.service. Commands that change
       something need root.

       **status** [__unit__...]
              without units: overall state and failed units; with units: state,
              main PID, command and the last lines of the output
       **list** [**-a**]   loaded units; **-a** also the inactive ones
       **list-files**     unit files on disk
       **start**, **stop**, **restart** __unit__...
              waits until the units settle and reports a failure
       **kill** __unit__  SIGKILL to the main process (it restarts if Restart= says so)
       **enable**, **disable** [**--now**] __unit__...
              create or remove the marker in /etc/init/system/TARGET.wants for
              every WantedBy= target; **--now** also starts or stops it
       **mask**, **unmask** __unit__  an empty /etc/init/system/UNIT blocks it completely
       **cat** __unit__   print the unit file
       **log** [**-n** __N__] __unit__  last lines of /var/log/init/UNIT.log
       **is-active**, **is-failed** __unit__
       **daemon-reload**  read unit files again
       **isolate** __target__  start the target, stop everything it does not want
       **get-default**, **set-default** __target__
       **poweroff**, **reboot**, **halt**

EXAMPLES
           initctl status netd
           initctl enable --now getty@tty7
           initctl set-default graphical.target

SEE ALSO
       init(8)
